.TH PVE\-BUILD\-WINDOWS\-TEMPLATE 8 "2026-08-05" "1.4.0" "Proxmox VE Tools"

.SH NAME
pve\-build\-windows\-template \- build sysprepped, cloud\-init\-capable Windows Server templates on Proxmox VE

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-build\-windows\-template
.RB { \-\-iso
.IR PATH " | " \-\-eval
.IR RELEASE }
.RB [ \-\-edition
.IR core | desktop | both ]
.RB [ \-\-sku
.IR standard | datacenter ]
.RB [ \-\-storage
.IR NAME ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-build\-windows\-template
turns a Windows Server installation ISO into one or more sysprepped Proxmox VE
templates in a single non\-interactive run. No console interaction is required
at any point: the script generates an
.B Autounattend.xml
answer file, bakes it together with the virtio drivers and every in\-guest
payload onto a small generated ISO, drives a build VM to completion, and seals
the result with
.BR "qm template" .
.PP
By default it produces
.B two
templates per invocation \(em Server Core and Desktop Experience \(em at
consecutive VMIDs starting at
.BR \-\-start\-id .
.PP
The output is a genuine template rather than a golden disk: Cloudbase\-Init is
installed and configured against the PVE cloud\-init drive, so a clone receives
its hostname, network configuration, administrator password and SSH keys on
first boot, exactly as a Linux clone does.

.SS Licensing
The script
.B never
downloads, caches or redistributes Windows media or a licence key. The operator
supplies the ISO with
.BR \-\-iso .
The single exception is opt\-in: passing
.B \-\-eval
downloads Microsoft's freely\-redistributable 180\-day evaluation media from the
Microsoft Evaluation Center. Only the virtio\-win driver ISO, the SPICE agent MSI
and Cloudbase\-Init \(em all redistributable \(em are fetched automatically, and
each can be overridden for air\-gapped sites.
.PP
Product keys are never downloaded and never appear in
.BR \-\-dry\-run
output, diagnostics or, in remote mode, the remote process table.

.SS Modes of operation
.TP
.B LOCAL
Run directly on a PVE node, as root.
.TP
.B REMOTE
Run from a jump host and give the node with
.BR \-S .
The script copies itself to the node and re\-executes there. The template stays
on the node \(em nothing is downloaded back. All paths
.RB ( \-\-iso ", " \-\-cache\-dir )
are interpreted
.BR remotely .
Only
.BR ssh (1)
and
.BR scp (1)
are needed on the jump host.

.SS Build sequence
.IP 1. 4
Resolve the Windows media, the virtio\-win ISO, the Cloudbase\-Init MSI and
the SPICE agent MSI, caching each under the ISO storage.
.IP 2. 4
Mount the Windows media (UDF) and read the image list with
.BR wiminfo (1)
to auto\-detect the release, detect evaluation media, and resolve the exact
.I /IMAGE/NAME
for the requested SKU and edition.
.IP 3. 4
Flatten the release\-specific virtio drivers and stage every in\-guest payload
onto a generated answer ISO. The build VM therefore needs
.B no
network access.
.IP 4. 4
Create the build VM \(em
.BR ovmf ", " q35 ", " virtio\-scsi\-single ,
a TPM 2.0 state volume and pre\-enrolled Secure Boot keys \(em and start it.
.IP 5. 4
Wait for Windows Setup, then for the in\-guest payload installation reported
through the QEMU guest agent, then for sysprep's own shutdown.
.IP 6. 4
Verify offline that
.I Sysprep_succeeded.tag
exists on the disk, detach every CD\-ROM, attach the cloud\-init drive and run
.BR "qm template" .

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Media
.TP
.BI \-i " PATH" "\fR, \fP" \-\-iso " PATH"
Windows installation ISO, given either as a filesystem path or as a
.IR STORAGE :iso/ NAME
volume identifier. Never downloaded automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-eval " RELEASE"
Download the Microsoft 180\-day evaluation ISO for
.IR RELEASE " (" 2019 " | " 2022 " | " 2025 ).
Ignored when
.B \-\-iso
is given.
.TP
.BI \-R " REL" "\fR, \fP" \-\-release " REL"
.IR 2019 " | " 2022 " | " 2025 .
Auto\-detected from the media when omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-virtio\-iso " PATH"
Use this virtio\-win ISO instead of downloading the stable build.
.TP
.BI \-\-cloudbase\-msi " PATH"
Use this Cloudbase\-Init MSI instead of downloading it.
.TP
.BI \-\-spice\-msi " PATH"
Use this SPICE vdagent MSI instead of downloading it. The default is
spice\-vdagent\-x64\-0.10.0.msi from spice\-space.org; upstream publishes no
"latest" alias for it, so the version is pinned.

.SS What to build
.TP
.BI \-e " WHICH" "\fR, \fP" \-\-edition " WHICH"
.IR core " | " desktop " | " both .
Default:
.BR both .
.TP
.BI \-k " SKU" "\fR, \fP" \-\-sku " SKU"
.IR standard " | " datacenter .
Default:
.BR standard .
.TP
.BI \-I " ID" "\fR, \fP" \-\-start\-id " ID"
First VMID. One VMID is consumed per edition, consecutively. Default:
.BR 9020 .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Destroy an existing VMID instead of skipping it.

.SS Placement and sizing
.TP
.BI \-s " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-storage " NAME"
Storage for VM disks. Default:
.BR local\-lvm .
.TP
.BI \-\-iso\-storage " NAME"
Storage for downloaded and generated ISOs. Must accept
.B iso
content. Default:
.BR \-\-storage .
.TP
.BI \-B " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-bridge " NAME"
Bridge for the finished template's NIC. Default:
.BR vmbr0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-vlan " TAG"
VLAN tag for the template NIC.
.TP
.BI \-\-build\-bridge " NAME"
Bridge for the build VM. Defaults to
.BR \-\-bridge .
An uplink\-less bridge is recommended so Windows Update cannot interfere with
the build.
.TP
.BI \-D " GB" "\fR, \fP" \-\-disk\-size " GB"
OS disk size. Default:
.BR 60 .
.TP
.BI \-c " TYPE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-cpu\-type " TYPE"
CPU model. Default:
.BR x86\-64\-v2\-AES ,
which is migration\-safe and sufficient for Server 2025 (POPCNT + SSE4.2).
.BR host " and " max
are deliberately not the default \(em they break live migration.
.TP
.BI \-\-cores " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-memory " MB"
Template sizing. Defaults:
.BR 2 " and " 4096 .
.TP
.BI \-\-build\-cores " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-build\-memory " MB"
Build VM sizing. Defaults:
.BR 4 " and " 8192 .
.TP
.BI \-\-vga " TYPE"
.IR std " | " qxl " | " virtio .
Default:
.BR std .
See
.B LIMITATIONS
regarding SPICE.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tpm
Do not attach a TPM 2.0 state volume.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-secureboot
Do not pre\-enrol the Microsoft Secure Boot keys.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rdp
Do not enable Remote Desktop. By default the template has Remote Desktop
switched on with its firewall rule opened.

.SS Windows configuration
.TP
.BI \-\-locale " TAG"
System and UI locale. Defaults to the language of the supplied media, read
from the WIM
.IR "Default Language" .
See
.BR "LANGUAGE SUPPORT" .
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-locale " TAG"
Keyboard layout. Defaults to
.BR \-\-locale .
.TP
.BI \-\-timezone " TZ"
Windows time zone name (these identifiers are language\-invariant). Default:
.BR UTC .
With
.B UTC
the VM is given an RTC in UTC
.RB ( "\-\-localtime 0" )
and Cloudbase\-Init is told the same through
.IR real_time_clock_utc ,
so the two agree. Any other zone keeps PVE's default local\-time RTC, which
is what Windows expects.
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-password " PW" "\fR, \fP" \-\-admin\-password\-file " FILE"
Administrator password baked into the template. When neither is given a random
18\-character password is generated and printed once. A clone keeps this
password until
.B \-\-cipassword
replaces it on first boot.
.TP
.BI \-\-ci\-username " NAME"
The account Cloudbase\-Init manages on clones. Default:
.BR Administrator .

.SS Activation
Supplying no key at all is valid \(em the install then runs in evaluation or
deferred\-activation mode and the operator activates after deployment.
.TP
.BI \-\-product\-key " KEY" "\fR, \fP" \-\-product\-key\-file " FILE"
Operator\-supplied key, embedded in the answer file and masked in all output.
.TP
.B \-\-kms
Use the public Microsoft KMS client setup key (GVLK) for this release and SKU.
Rejected on evaluation media, where a GVLK cannot activate.
.TP
.BI \-\-kms\-host " HOST[:PORT]"
Record a KMS server in the Cloudbase\-Init configuration so clones activate
against it on first boot. The GVLK itself is still baked in at build time by
.BR \-\-kms .

.SS Caching, timeouts and diagnostics
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " DIR"
Payload cache. Default:
.IR <iso\-storage> /pve\-tools\-cache/windows\-templates .
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-cache
Re\-download cached media.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-answer\-iso
Keep the generated answer ISO. It contains the administrator password and any
product key in cleartext, so it is deleted by default.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-on\-failure
Leave the build VM in place when a build fails, for interactive inspection.
.TP
.BI \-\-install\-timeout " S" "\fR, \fP" \-\-payload\-timeout " S" "\fR, \fP" \-\-sysprep\-timeout " S"
Per\-phase timeouts in seconds. Defaults:
.BR 3600 ", " 1800 ", " 1800 .
.TP
.B \-\-show\-answer\-file
Print the generated
.B Autounattend.xml
with secrets redacted.

.SS General
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-mode " MODE"
.IR local " | " remote .
Defaults to
.B local
unless
.B \-S
is given.
.TP
.BI \-S " USER@HOST" "\fR, \fP" \-\-server " USER@HOST"
Remote mode \(em target PVE node.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the full plan and touch nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the script version.

.SH TEMPLATE NAMING
Sealed templates are named
.IP
.EX
ci\-win<release>\-<std|dc>\-<core|desktop>\-<locale>\-<timestamp>.x86\-64
.EE
.PP
for example
.IR ci\-win2025\-std\-core\-ja\-jp\-202608051603.x86\-64 .
The locale is lowercased so the name stays a valid DNS label, which PVE
requires. It is part of the name because without it two localisations of the
same release, SKU and edition are distinguished only by the timestamp, which
has minute resolution and is taken once per run: two builds starting in the
same minute would produce identical names. The locale is also recorded in the
template description.
.SH LANGUAGE SUPPORT
Any Windows Server localisation is supported with no extra arguments.
.PP
.B \-\-eval
covers only the eight languages Microsoft publishes evaluation media in:
en\-US, fr\-FR, es\-ES, de\-DE, it\-IT, ja\-JP, ru\-RU and zh\-CN. Anything
else, ko\-KR and zh\-TW included, is rejected by name. The Evaluation Center
answers an unrecognised
.I clcid
with the English ISO and an HTTP 200, giving no indication of the
substitution, so accepting those values would produce an English template
labelled with another language. Supply such media yourself with
.BR \-\-iso .
As a second line of defence, if
.B \-\-eval
media arrives in a language other than the one requested, the build stops.
.TP
.B Edition selection is language\-invariant
The script matches the WIM
.I Name
field, which Microsoft does not localise \(em Spanish media still reports
.IR "Windows Server 2025 SERVERSTANDARDCORE" .
The localised strings live in
.IR "Display Name" ,
which the script deliberately ignores.
.TP
.B The release comes from the NT build number
.IR 17763 " \(-> 2019, " 20348 " \(-> 2022, " 26100 " \(-> 2025,"
rather than an English product string.
.B \-\-release
overrides it.
.TP
.B \-\-locale defaults to the media's own language
Read from the WIM
.IR "Default Language" .
.I SetupUILanguage
must name a language present on the media, so a fixed
.B en\-US
default would break every non\-English ISO. Passing a
.B \-\-locale
the media does not carry produces a warning before the build starts.
.TP
.B The Remote Desktop firewall rule uses an indirect reference
.I @FirewallAPI.dll,\-28752
rather than the display name
.RB \(dq "Remote Desktop" \(dq,
which is localised and would not match on a non\-English install.
.PP
One caveat:
.I groups=Administrators
in the Cloudbase\-Init configuration is a literal group name, and on a
localised Windows the local group is
.IR Administradores ", " Администраторы
and so on. It is only consulted when
.B \-\-ci\-username
names an account that does not already exist; the default
.B Administrator
is already a member, so the common path is unaffected.

.SH CLOUD-INIT ON WINDOWS
Proxmox VE presents cloud\-init to Windows guests as an OpenStack config\-drive
.RB ( citype " " configdrive2 ,
the default for any Windows
.BR ostype ).
The generated Cloudbase\-Init configuration uses
.B ConfigDriveService
accordingly. Three behaviours differ from a Linux template and are worth
knowing before you clone:
.TP
.B \-\-ciuser is a no\-op
Cloudbase\-Init acts on the account named in its own configuration file, not on
anything from the metadata. The managed account is fixed at build time by
.BR \-\-ci\-username " (default " Administrator ).
.TP
.B \-\-cipassword works
It reaches the guest as
.I admin_pass
in
.I meta_data.json
and is applied to the managed account. Note that
.B qm cloudinit dump <id> meta
does not show it: that subcommand renders the generic config\-drive metadata
rather than the Cloudbase\-Init variant PVE actually generates for Windows
guests.
.B \-\-sshkeys
works the same way and lands in
.IR C:\e\eUsers\e\e<ci\-username>\e\e.ssh\e\eauthorized_keys ,
but Windows Server ships no SSH server, so the keys are inert until the
OpenSSH Server feature is installed.
.TP
.B Hostname arrives through user_data, not meta_data
PVE's Windows
.I meta_data.json
carries no
.I hostname
key, so
.B UserDataPlugin
is mandatory in the plugin list \(em it is what feeds the cloud\-config
.I hostname
through to
.BR SetHostNamePlugin .
Removing it from
.I cloudbase\-init.conf
silently breaks
.BR "qm clone \-\-name" .

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build Core and Desktop Standard templates from an operator\-supplied ISO:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
pve\-build\-windows\-template \-\-iso dstore01:iso/win2022.iso \-\-storage dstore01
.EE
.RE
.PP
Evaluation media, Datacenter, Core only, built on an isolated bridge:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
pve\-build\-windows\-template \-\-eval 2025 \-\-sku datacenter \-\-edition core \\
    \-\-storage dstore01 \-\-build\-bridge vmbr1 \-\-start\-id 9040
.EE
.RE
.PP
Licensed media activated against a KMS server:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
pve\-build\-windows\-template \-\-iso /mnt/iso/win2022\-vl.iso \-\-kms \\
    \-\-storage dstore01
.EE
.RE
.PP
Remote build from a jump host (paths are interpreted on the node):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
pve\-build\-windows\-template \-\-iso dstore01:iso/win2022.iso \\
    \-\-storage dstore01 \-S root@pve1.example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Clone the resulting template:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
qm clone 9020 130 \-\-name winsrv01 \-\-full
qm set 130 \-\-ipconfig0 ip=10.0.0.30/24,gw=10.0.0.1 \-\-nameserver 10.0.0.1
qm set 130 \-\-cipassword 'secret' \-\-sshkeys ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
qm start 130
.EE
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.IR <iso\-storage> /template/iso/
Downloaded evaluation and virtio\-win ISOs, and the generated
.I pve\-answer\-*.iso
(removed after each build unless
.BR \-\-keep\-answer\-iso ).
.TP
.IR <iso\-storage> /pve\-tools\-cache/windows\-templates/
Cloudbase\-Init and SPICE agent installers. Override with
.BR \-\-cache\-dir .
.TP
.I C:\e\epvebuild\e\estate.txt
In\-guest build progress log, preserved on the finished template for
post\-mortem analysis.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested templates were built and verified.
.TP
.B 1
A validation, download, build or verification step failed. The build VM is
destroyed unless
.B \-\-keep\-on\-failure
was given; diagnostics from
.IR state.txt ,
.I Panther\e\esetupact.log
and the sysprep log are printed first.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
On the PVE node: Proxmox VE 8.x or later,
.BR genisoimage (1)
or
.BR mkisofs (1),
.BR wiminfo (1)
from
.IR wimtools ,
.BR guestfish (1)
from
.IR libguestfs\-tools ,
.BR curl (1)
and
.BR python3 (1).
In remote mode the jump host needs only
.BR ssh (1)
and
.BR scp (1).

.SH LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Windows Server only \(em desktop Windows editions are not supported.
.IP \(bu 2
UEFI/GPT only. BIOS/MBR installs are not supported.
.IP \(bu 2
Domain join at build time is out of scope; it belongs at clone time.
.IP \(bu 2
Cloud\-init addressing is only reliable for a single NIC, or for several NICs of
the same model. PVE's Windows config\-drive writes the network configuration as
Debian ENI with no MAC address
.RB ( cloudbase_network_eni ()
in
.IR PVE/QemuServer/Cloudinit.pm ),
so Cloudbase\-Init assigns
.BR \-\-ipconfig0 ,
.BR \-\-ipconfig1 ,
\&... in Windows adapter\-enumeration order rather than by identity. Two virtio
NICs added in order enumerate in the same order and map correctly. Mixed models
do not: a clone with
.B net0
e1000 plus
.BR net1 / net2
virtio received all three addresses rotated onto the wrong adapters, because
Windows enumerates the virtio adapters ahead of the e1000. Give extra NICs their
addresses by other means. Adding NICs, disks or other hardware to a clone is
otherwise unrestricted; only cloud\-init's automatic addressing is affected.
.IP \(bu 2
Cloudbase\-Init is always installed; there is no
.B \-\-no\-cloudbase\-init
escape hatch in this release.
.IP \(bu 2
On Server Core, Device Manager reports one undriveable
.B PCI Device
.RB ( 8086:293E ,
the ICH9 HD Audio controller). PVE's q35 machine definition attaches it to
every VM and Server Core ships no audio driver. It is cosmetic and is neither
added nor removable by this script.
.IP \(bu 2
The virtio\-win
.B qxldod
display driver has no INF for Server 2022 or 2025, so
.B \-\-vga std
is the default. The SPICE agent is installed regardless \(em the display type is
a clone\-time decision made with
.BR "qm set <id> \-\-vga qxl" .
Note that the
.B spice\-agent
service is registered to start automatically but only stays running while a
SPICE display is actually attached, so it reads
.B Stopped
on a
.B \-\-vga std
clone. That is correct behaviour, not a failed install.
.IP \(bu 2
The virtio\-win ISO must be new enough for the target release. The script
refuses to build rather than producing a broken template.
.IP \(bu 2
Windows Server 2025 Setup appends a WinRE recovery partition after the system
volume whatever partition layout the answer file specifies, which would leave
.B C:
unextendable. The build disables WinRE and reclaims that partition before
sealing, so
.B qm resize
behaves the same on every supported release.

